  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 328 AM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nThe upper level trough which helped usher in cooler temperatures \nearlier will continue shifting east while ridging aloft builds into \nthe region from the west through the day. As this ridge builds in \nexpect lighter winds and temperatures a bit warmer this afternoon.\n\nCritically low afternoon minimum relative humidity values through \nthe week will allow for fire danger concerns to persist for several \ndays. Please continue to monitor the latest forecast and outlook, as \nappropriate fire weather hazards/products may need adjustments to \nareal coverage and intensity day to day, particularly through the \nwork week. Lighter winds throughout the week will mitigate against a \nhigher fire weather threat. \n\nThis surface high and increased ridging aloft from upstream will \nensure weather conditions for the week remain calm and quiet, with \ntemperatures raising daily. \n\nFire weather concerns remain the most significant factor so far this \nweek. Fires may rapidly spread once started due to dry fuels./OAJ/",
